.env
profile.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real lead data — NEVER COMMIT.
#
# These files hold other people's names and working email addresses, collected
# from company websites and Hunter.io. They are not yours to publish: a public
# repo is indexed and scraped within days, and a deletion does not reach the
# forks, clones and caches that already have it.
#
# Only the sample_*.csv files below are safe to commit. Everything else that
# comes out of this pipeline is somebody's contact details.
#
# If you add a new output file, add it here FIRST.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

startups_clean.csv
custom.csv
verified.csv
outreach.csv
outreach_*.csv
research.csv
campaign.csv

# Catch-alls for anything derived from the above.
*_leads.csv
*_verified.csv
*_emails.csv

# Your own application letter, if you keep a filled-in copy separately.
template.arnav.txt
template.previous.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicitly allowed: the synthetic samples a fresh clone runs on.
# Every domain in these is under example.com/.org/.net (RFC 2606 reserved),
# so no address in them can ever belong to a real person.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!sample_startups.csv
!sample_custom.csv
!profile.example.json

